<article class="env-lemma" id="08SK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08SK">Lemma <span data-tag="08SK">92.14.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a surjective ring map whose kernel $I$ is Koszul. Then $L_{B/A}$ is quasi-isomorphic to $I/I^2[1]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Locally on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ the ideal $I$ is generated by a Koszul regular sequence, see More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/07CV" data-tag="07CV">15.33.1</a>. Hence this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/08QQ" data-tag="08QQ">92.6.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>